  "schematicNotes": [
    {
      "id": "n_cavity_notes",
      "text": "CAVITY NOTES - full text of the signals marked * on this drawing\nBulkhead A - engine plug (HDP2 1: spare (size 16) - was the shared shield drain, retired by 6.32\nBulkhead A - engine plug (HDP2 35: MRS EPS pump logic enable - cabin fuse block c14 (7.5A, ignition-switched); moved from bulkhead B c14 2026-09-28 (the pump's ECU signal is A27); engine-side wire on ST185-EngineRoom-C (broken off)\nBulkhead A - engine plug (HDP2 36: Aux 7 MRS speed-out (ECU A27) - engine-side wire on ST185-EngineRoom-C (broken off)",
      "schematicPosition": {
        "x": 4200,
        "y": 0
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "n_sp_gndout_fit",
      "text": "sp_gndout_eng SPLICE FIT: four 20 AWG wires = one 14 AWG combined (Wire Barn Combined Wire Gauge Calculator, https://www.wirebarn.com/Combined-Wire-Gauge-Calculator_ep_42.html), inside the GENERIC CRIMP SPLICE 14-10 range. Splices are sized by combined gauge (Daniel 2026-09-28). harness.design's per-wire 'wires are too thin' warning on this splice is a known false alarm.",
      "width": 390,
      "schematicPosition": {
        "x": 1980,
        "y": 780
      }
    }
  ],
